WEBVTT

NOTE
Narration of the Agent Kourier demo (docs/brand/film/narration.json, "demo").
Cue times read from the 16:9 render with ffmpeg silencedetect.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.750
You've put AI agents on Kubernetes.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.450
They can read logs, check rollouts,
and find the cause.

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:11.050
But they sit behind a prompt,
away from where your team works.

4
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.450
Alerts and questions land in team chat.

5
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:19.350
Putting your agent there means building threads,
streaming and questions yourself.

6
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.650
Introducing Agent Kourier:

7
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.250
a Kubernetes-native broker between team chat
and streaming A2A agents.

8
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.750
An alert, or a question, becomes an agent session
in its own thread.

9
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.550
Your alerts arrive in the channel
as they always have.

10
00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.900
Agent Kourier reads each one
and hands it to your agent.

11
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.350
The agent investigates under the alert,
step by step.

12
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.250
Reply in the thread, and the session continues
with everything it already found.

13
00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.100
No alert? Mention Agent Kourier and ask.

14
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:07.100
When the agent needs a decision,
it asks, and waits for your answer.

15
00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:14.650
In Microsoft Teams, the agent works the alert
step by step too.

16
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.000
Teams support is experimental.

17
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.500
Webhooks start sessions too.

18
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:25.400
A pull request opens, and the agent reviews it
on GitHub with its own tools.

19
00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.450
A team applies a Binding next to its agent.

20
00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:31.600
The agent needs no chat code.

21
00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:38.150
Agent Kourier works with kagent,
or any A2A agent that streams.

22
00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:44.150
It keeps a session per thread, streams the reply,
and carries the agent's questions and your answers.

23
00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:48.300
Slack is supported;
Microsoft Teams and webhooks are experimental.

24
00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:49.800
Agent Kourier.

25
00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.500
Write the agent, not the chat integration.
